* GKR, in plain words
** The problem
*** Someone did a huge calculation for you
*** Redoing it yourself takes just as long
*** GKR turns checking into a short question game

** Ingredient 1: the cookie game
*** Baker claims a total score
*** Each round splits the total in two halves
*** You pick a random number after the baker answers
*** Last round: you taste one single cookie
*** Cheating almost never survives all the rounds

** Ingredient 2: the smooth surface
*** A table of numbers becomes one smooth formula
*** Two different tables give two different formulas
*** Checking one random point checks the whole table

** Ingredient 3: the chocolate factory
*** Ingredients go in, chocolate bars come out
*** Each machine adds or multiplies two values
*** The wiring plan is public, the values are not

** The inspection game
*** Start at the packaging stage, the output
*** Play the cookie game at each stage
*** Line trick: two questions become one
*** Last stage: the inspector checks the raw materials herself

** Why it is fast
*** Inspector: a handful of checks per stage
*** Factory: a little more work than running the line
*** Messages: a few numbers per stage

** Keeping secrets
*** Add random noise that cancels out
*** Total still checks out, single values stay hidden

** Where it is used
*** Blockchain rollups that prove off-chain work
*** Proof libraries such as Spartan, Hyrax and Libra
*** Checking computations run on someone else's machine
